---
/** The play mark: a disc with a triangle on it, on the map's video triggers
    and on each video window's play button. It has no look of its own: whoever
    places it sizes it and fills its `circle` and `path`, styling them with
    `:global()`, since a page's scoped styles don't reach into another
    component. It's hidden from assistive tech, as the button round it says
    what it does. Its width and height give a page with no stylesheet a small
    mark, not a full-size one. */
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
  <circle cx="20" cy="20" r="20"></circle>
  <path d="M16 12.5v15l12-7.5z"></path>
</svg>
